Under Regulation Z, 12 CFR 1026.13 ( b ) ( 1 ), the 60-day period for reporting a billing error begins after the first periodic statement on which the error appeared is transmitted to the consumer. The CFPBs Official Interpretation clarifies that this deadline applies only once a consumer could reasonably identify an error from the information provided. Because the service failure was not apparent until months after billing, the alleged error was not discoverable within 60 days. 

Furthermore, Regulation Z 1026.13 ( f ) requires a reasonable investigation and a fair opportunity for the consumer to present information. Reliance on a single unconfirmed email that went to spam does not constitute reasonable notice. 

I am requesting that Capital One be directed to reopen or reinvestigate the dispute, review the documentation I have supplied, and issue a written explanation of findings in compliance with Regulation Z and the Fair Credit Billing Act.",,CAPITAL ONE FINANCIAL CORPORATION,CA,92694,,Web,2025-11-03,Closed with explanation,Yes
