17350884,2025-11-20,Debt collection,Rental debt,False statements or representation,Attempted to collect wrong amount,"I am disputing an alleged rental debt that XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX forwarded to XXXX XXXX. The balance is inaccurate and includes charges that are unlawful under Texas Property Code 92.10492.109. 

My tenancy at XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX ended on XX/XX/XXXX. Before moving out, the property acknowledged in writing that I had overpaid my final months rent by {$360.00}, yet this amount was never refunded. My {$400.00} security deposit was also withheld and applied to cleaning, painting, and carpet charges that represent ordinary wear and tear, not tenant-caused damage. Under Texas law, landlords can not deduct these items from a security deposit. 

Equity Residential also billed me for utilities after my lease ended, which I do not owe. They then claimed I owed an additional balance and forwarded this incorrect amount to XXXX XXXX 

I disputed the debt in writing with XXXX and requested full validation. XXXX response did not meet FDCPA validation requirements. They did not provide : A copy of my signed lease Proof that XXXX XXXX  authorized them to collect this debt Evidence that I caused any damage beyond normal wear Receipts or invoices tied specifically to my unit Documentation showing my rent overpayment was credited Documentation showing my security deposit was handled legally Any explanation connecting the invoices to the charges they claim I owe The photos and inspection materials provided show only routine cleaning needs, not damage. Nothing supports the charges assessed. 

