17420885,2025-11-21,Mortgage,Conventional home mortgage,Trouble during payment process,Payment process,"My mortgage was recently transferred to RoundPoint Mortgage. Since the transfer, they have mishandled my payments and are incorrectly charging me a late fee.

For years, I have consistently paid my mortgage in two half-payments one on the XXXX and one on the XXXX of each month. Both payments are made before the due date, and my prior servicer always credited them properly without issue. 

RoundPoint informed me that their policy is to place my early half-payments into a suspense account until a full payment is accumulated. Because of this self-created policy, they are attempting to charge me a late fee and are pressuring me to enroll in their biweekly payment program, which I do not want. 

The representative told me that the CFPB only requires full payments to be collected and used this claim to justify placing my early payments in suspense. This contradicts federal law. Under 12 CFR 1026.36 ( c ) ( 1 ) and 12 CFR 1024.35 ( RESPA ) : Servicers must credit payments as of the date received.

Servicers can not impose late fees resulting from payment misapplication.

Consumers have a 60-day grace period after a servicing transfer during which late fees and negative credit reporting are prohibited for any transfer-related issues. 

Servicers can not force a borrower into a different payment structure or penalize them for a payment schedule previously accepted by the prior servicer. 

RoundPoint is violating these rules by using its internal policy to override my established payment history, delay crediting my payments, and manufacture a late fee.

I am requesting CFPB assistance to : Remove the improper late fee Correct my payment history Confirm that my established XXXX and XXXX payment schedule will be accepted Confirm that RoundPoint can not require enrollment in a biweekly program I have paid on time and followed the same payment structure for years. This is a servicing error, and I request immediate correction under RESPA and Regulation X.",,RoundPoint Mortgage Servicing LLC,TX,77004,Servicemember,Web,2025-11-21,Closed with explanation,Yes
