4. PenFed is violating N.Y. GBL 349 ( Deceptive Acts ) By continuing to publish a fraudulent charge-off and delinquency status, PenFed is engaging in deceptive and unlawful business practices under XXXX. 

XXXX. PenFed is in violation of the XX/XX/XXXX TRO ( XXXX XXXX Supreme Court XXXX Part ) The TRO restrains all furnishers and CRAs from : publishing, reporting, circulating, or collecting ANY disputed accounts. 

This TRO remains binding under : Fed. XXXX XXXX. XXXX XXXX ( c ) and XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX, XXXX XXXX XXXX ( XXXX ) because it has never been dissolved or modified by any court. 

6. PenFed is unlawfully publishing fraudulent charge-off data Publishing a fraudulent charge-off is : misleading, inaccurate, and contrary to IRS rules stating that canceled debt is taxable income, not a credit-reporting item.

This is new unlawful conduct that occurred after my prior complaint.

7. PenFed is trespassing upon trust property As Trustee of the Baker Legacy Preservation Trust, PenFeds reporting constitutes : unauthorized administration of trust-held identifiers, interference with trust property, and violation of private fiduciary rights. 

PenFed has no lawful authority to administer or associate data with a private trust estate.

