This means the debt collector is : 1. Reporting unverifiable information 2. Failing to provide validation after repeated disputes 3. Continuing to furnish information that has not been proven accurate 4. Violating FCRA 602 ( A ) and FCRA 623 ( a ) ( 1 ) ( A ) by failing to ensure accuracy and completeness 5. Ignoring my written disputes submitted to the credit bureaus per FCRA 611 I requested validation, including the following : Original creditor name Itemized accounting of the amount claimed Proof of ownership / chain of title Signed contract or agreement Date of alleged default Notice of assignment or sale The collector has not provided any of these items.

Despite this, they continue to report the account, which is unverified, inaccurate, and incomplete. The credit bureaus are also failing to conduct a proper investigation, and the collector is continuing to furnish data that can not be substantiated.

I am requesting the CFPB to require : 1. The collector to provide full validation or immediately cease reporting the account.

2. The credit bureaus to remove the account if the collector can not verify it.

3. Documentation from the collector proving that they ever sent the legally required initial written notice.

I am seeking resolution because the continued reporting of an unverified and unvalidated debt is causing financial harm and violates federal law.

Thank you for your assistance.",,"EQUIFAX, INC.",WV,253XX,,Web,2025-11-25,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes
